parameter derivatives have also been controlled.  This is needed when the
physical spherical factor occurs in the inner conic region: repeated radial
integration by parts differentiates that factor, even though its frequency
need not be large.

The definitions below retain the actual middle cutoff.  Differentiating the
frequency parameter simply inserts another sine factor.  Consequently every
derivative is a compact meridian integral and has a uniform bound.  No
symbol-class regularity is assumed.
